@Patricia Henry

I dunno.  As I'm listening to it, my mind keeps going to Chicago's "Colour My World," which definitely has lyrics, and is sung.  

I do agree, however, that a great amount of cruciverbial license must be taken here to call Moonlight Sonata a "song."

@Googoo

My first thought was the group of nations assembled in 1975. 

Gulfstream came to mind only later.

@Jonathan Baldwin
Not to take anything away from your apt observation, Google did offer this:

Classical composers like Felix Mendelssohn explicitly wrote piano collections titled Songs Without Words (Lieder ohne Worte) to mimic vocal melodies on instruments.

